+          <p class="muted">Radius, static trim and drive shift the resonance. A closer gap strengthens coupling and broadens the loaded line. Intrinsic Q controls loss inside the ring. Watch the through and drop fractions as you sweep the probe across the resonance, then raise link loss to see how much power still reaches the detector.</p>
